Package: tachyon-firmware-dragonwing-compat
Version: 1.0~tachyon4
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Tachyon Platform <eugene@particle.io>
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Provides: linux-firmware-dragonwing (= 9999.0.0)
Conflicts: linux-firmware-dragonwing
Depends: tachyon-firmware
Description: Satisfy the linux-firmware-dragonwing dependency without shadowing platform firmware
 qcom-fastrpc1 - pulled in by the CamX camera stack - depends on
 linux-firmware-dragonwing. That upstream package ships 571 files, 381 of them
 under /lib/firmware/updates, a path the kernel searches ahead of
 /lib/firmware. Installing it would shadow the Particle-tuned blobs even
 without a Replaces relationship.
 .
 The wifi adapter here is PCI 17cb:1103 and the driver asks for it as
 qca6698aq hw2.1, loading from ath11k/QCA6698AQ/hw2.1/. Both packages populate
 that name, but in opposite directions:
 .
   tachyon-firmware   QCA6698AQ -> WCN6855, whose contents are symlinks into
                      /vendor/wlan on the read-only BP partition
   dragonwing         real WCN6855/hw2.1/* files, plus QCA6698AQ -> WCN6855
 .
 Because both own the WCN6855 path, a plain install stops there with a file
 conflict. Forced through, the active QCA6698AQ requests would resolve to
 dragonwing's WCN6855 blobs instead of the Particle ones - and losing wifi
 means losing the only remote access to the board.
 .
 fastrpc only needs the CDSP firmware, which the board already carries. This
 package satisfies the dependency and declares Conflicts so the upstream
 package can never be co-installed, keeping tachyon-firmware the sole provider.
 .
 It ships no firmware of its own. The blobs come from tachyon-firmware and the
 add-qcm6490-bp-fw overlay, and /vendor must be mounted from the initramfs
 before the consuming drivers probe.
